# DataGuard Gemini Rules

- Use `AGENTS.md` and `rules/workspace_governance.md` as the workspace authority.
- Production source is `src/`; use DataGuard .NET build/test evidence before claiming a source change is complete.
- Keep docs, plans, research, grants, strategy, automation, and local runtime state in their defined boundaries.
- Update user-facing documentation from verified facts when its contract changes; do not invent commands, deployment status, or test output.
- Do not remove tracked files, legal text, research, agent config, cache, or session state from a missing-reference search alone.
- Cleanup requires a preserved-WIP, owner-approved `from → keep | extract | rewrite | remove` manifest.
- Never disclose credentials, tokens, secrets, or private handoff/session data.

